`the pensioners' tables of 2018` MEANS
    LIST `pensioners' table 1 of 2018`, `pensioners' table 2 of 2018`, `pensioners' table 3 of 2018`, `pensioners' table 4 of 2018`, `pensioners' table 6 of 2018`, `pensioners' table 7 of 2018`, `pensioners' table 8 of 2018`

-- The month annex 4 prints illegible: the last row's ("[לא קריא].202").
`why the pensioners' tables' illegible month of 2018 is not here` MEANS
    `the text is missing` "נספח 4 (טבלת גמלאים דירוג מינהלי), השורה האחרונה: החודש לא קריא"

§§ `בדיקת טבלאות הגמלאים`

-- (1) Every table: 83 rows, the months 1.2013 to 11.2019 in order — each
-- printed month and year is its row's — and the printed number is the
-- month's count, to 60 (five years).
GIVEN i IS A NUMBER, r IS A `pensioners' row of 2018`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prints the month of its place` i r IF
        (r's `the printed number of 2018` EQUALS (IF i PLUS 1 GREATER THAN 60 THEN 60 ELSE i PLUS 1))
    AND (r's `the printed month of 2018` EQUALS NOTHING OR r's `the printed month of 2018` EQUALS JUST ((i MODULO 12) PLUS 1))
    AND (r's `the printed year of 2018` EQUALS NOTHING OR r's `the printed year of 2018` EQUALS JUST (2013 PLUS FLOOR (i DIVIDED BY 12)))

GIVEN t IS A LIST OF `pensioners' row of 2018`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `runs from 1.2013 to 11.2019` t IF
        count t EQUALS 83
    AND and (zipWith `prints the month of its place` (range 0 82) t)

#ASSERT all `runs from 1.2013 to 11.2019` `the pensioners' tables of 2018`

-- (2) Each running total is the total before it and the stage's part, to a
-- hundredth of a point (each is rounded on the page), and the last is X in
-- all.
GIVEN before IS A NUMBER, cs IS A LIST OF MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the totals run on from` before cs IS
    CONSIDER cs
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER rest
        WHEN t FOLLOWED BY more THEN
            CONSIDER p
            WHEN JUST part THEN
                CONSIDER t
                WHEN JUST total THEN total `is within a hundredth of a point of` (before PLUS part) AND `the totals run on from` total more
                WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN t EQUALS NOTHING AND `the totals run on from` before more
        WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE

GIVEN r IS A `pensioners' row of 2018`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `adds up to X in all` r IF
        (CONSIDER r's `the stage cells of 2018`
         WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `the totals run on from` (fromMaybe 0 first) rest
         WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE)
    AND at (r's `the stage cells of 2018`) (count (r's `the stage cells of 2018`) MINUS 1) EQUALS JUST (r's `X in all of 2018`)

#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD all `adds up to X in all` t) (drop 1 `the pensioners' tables of 2018`)

-- Annex 1's rows 6.2018 to 7.2019 print the total to December 2019 as the
-- last part alone, 24.05%, where X in all is 46.20% and the row's two parts
-- (22.15% and 24.05%) make it; the corpus marks the cells [כך במקור], and
-- the reading takes X in all, which (3) below holds to the frame's rule.
`the rows of annex 1 of 2018 that do not add up` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD NOT `adds up to X in all` r) `pensioners' table 1 of 2018`

#ASSERT count `the rows of annex 1 of 2018 that do not add up` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD r's `X in all of 2018` EQUALS 46.20%) `the rows of annex 1 of 2018 that do not add up`

-- (3) Annex 1, the framework's own: X in all is the share of the frame the
-- retiree earned while serving — a sixtieth a month, to five years — less
-- the share allocated by the first of his last month, under the steps as
-- amended here (7.9% in all), to a hundredth of a point.
GIVEN i IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `X in all under the frame of 2018 for the month at` i IS
    `not below zero`
        ((IF i PLUS 1 GREATER THAN 60 THEN 1 ELSE (i PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 60)
         MINUS `the 2016 framework allocation as amended in 2018 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 ((i MODULO 12) PLUS 1) (2013 PLUS FLOOR (i DIVIDED BY 12)))
               DIVIDED BY `the 2016 framework cost frame in all, as amended in 2018`)

#ASSERT and (zipWith (GIVEN i, r YIELD (r's `X in all of 2018`) `is within a hundredth of a point of` (`X in all under the frame of 2018 for the month at` i))
                     (range 0 82) `pensioners' table 1 of 2018`)
